curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:7777/v1/chat \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "tier": "standard",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "diga oi em 5 palavras"}]
  }' | jq

Pra testar /v1/tool/bash
Daemon roda (kill old, fresh start). Em outro terminal:

1. Caso feliz — git status no kira repo
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:7777/v1/tool/bash \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "argv": ["git", "status", "--short"],
    "cwd": "/Users/avanade/Workspace/kira"
  }' | jq
Esperado: stdout com git status output, exit_code: 0, duration_ms curto.

2. Allowlist block — executável proibido
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:7777/v1/tool/bash \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"argv": ["rm", "-rf", "/"]}' | jq
Esperado: HTTP 500 com erro: "executable 'rm' not in allowlist (SC3)".

3. Arg regex block — metacaracter
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:7777/v1/tool/bash \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"argv": ["ls", "; cat /etc/passwd"]}' | jq
Esperado: erro: "arg #0 '; cat /etc/passwd' contains forbidden chars".

4. Timeout
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:7777/v1/tool/bash \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"argv": ["find", "/"], "timeout_secs": 2}' | jq
Esperado: erro: "bash tool timed out after 2s" (find / não termina em 2s).

5. Path traversal protegido (cwd canonicalize)
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:7777/v1/tool/bash \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"argv": ["pwd"], "cwd": "/etc/../etc/passwd"}' | jq
Esperado: erro porque /etc/passwd é arquivo (canonicalize falha em cd).
